ce the change to G2: the protocol is frozen with the lint control and no unit control.\"\n+    root_cause: >\n+      `detectNodeStack` (`src/application/stacks/node.ts`) declares a control per readable script and\n+      reports the refused runner apart, in `capability_missing`. `designVerification`\n+      (`src/application/phases/verification-design.ts`) reads `capability_missing` as a refusal only\n+      when `controls` is empty. Introduced by the branch, which made a runner other than node:test\n+      and vitest a refusal instead of a node:test run.\n+    evidence: >\n+      A throwaway probe of `detectStack` on the package above returned `controls: [\"lint\"]` and\n+      `capability_missing: [\"scripts.test runs jest, whose output 495 cannot read: ...\"]`; the reading\n+      of `designVerification` shows the only `CAPABILITY_MISSING` raise guarded by\n+      `detection.controls.length === 0`.\n+    risk_level: medium\n+    follow_ups: >\n+      Decide whether a refused `scripts.test` stops the design of the protocol whatever the other\n+      controls, or is offered to the owner as an insufficiency to accept; either adds a refusal or a\n+      dialog, so it is a product decision.\n+    status: open\ncommit 1bf26b66f6c4ab1ee6a2428aebb94cf6da2177e9\nAuthor: jeanjerome <jeanjerome.levy@gmail.com>\nDate:   Tue Sep 29 13:47:17 2026 +0200\n\n    docs: the registry records that the Seatbelt test of the generic runner grants the temporary directory and so cannot fail under it\n\ndiff --git a/specs/bugs/registry.yaml b/specs/bugs/registry.yaml\nindex 134e3ea..5cb117c 100644\n--- a/specs/bugs/registry.yaml\n+++ b/specs/bugs/registry.yaml\n@@ -1250,3 +1250,32 @@ bugs:\n     follow_ups: \"none\"\n     status: fixed\n     fixed_in: bd10032\n+  - bug_id: BUG-2026-09-29T160000\n+    date: \"2026-09-29\"\n+    title: \"The Seatbelt test of the generic runner cannot fail when the repository lives under the temporary directory\"\n+    severity: low\n+    priority: p3\n+    s